  "notes": {
    "cc1_build": "2026-09-26 Q17 unpatch (owner ruling: 'consider a compiler patch a cheat'): build/cc1 = `bash tools/build_oracle_cc1.sh --install` = pinned upstream decompals/mips-gcc-2.7.2@43d1cdb67ed135879869b5266f01efaaada5e35a + tools/cc1-reorg-negate-rtx-decl.patch (host-only crash fix, no codegen change) and NOTHING else; tools/cc1-plus-to-ior-narrow.patch is SUPERSEDED, not applied. Recipe all -O0 -g, combine.o -O, -fgnu89-inline (host gcc 13, x86_64). sha1 ac80146bf50af58f719868de74c860fcdf617d30, simplify_rtx 0x3a11 (stock). Previous narrow binary aa04d761 kept as build/cc1.PRE-RECIPE-aa04d761; self-check vs it: no TU differs (func_800174F4, its only dependent, returned to INCLUDE_ASM in the same change). Diagnostic tools/gcc-2.7.2/cc1 rebuilt without the patch: 3f796363f33649712006f2eefb47c2f8c4539ffc, agrees on every TU. Verified: FULL BUILD SHA1 == 62efab4f73f992798c43e8c730aa43baa10bb4fa (verify-oracle --rebuild); every C object byte-identical to the pre-swap build except ings.o; engine test 801/801; fixtures 5/5; check_completion_integrity OK.",
    "cc1_build_2026_08_24": "2026-08-24 crash-fix rebuild (owner ruling, decisions.md 'cc1 fork-crash fix'): source = tmp/cc1build tree + one-line negate_rtx PROTO declaration in reorg.c (64-bit-host implicit-int pointer truncation; same fix mirrored in tools/gcc-2.7.2/reorg.c). Host build: `make cc1` in tmp/cc1build \u2014 cc -DCROSS_COMPILE -DIN_GCC -g (gcc 13, x86_64). Verified: 9/9 crash probes compile; codegen identical on all previously-OK probes; FULL BUILD SHA1 == 62efab4f73f992798c43e8c730aa43baa10bb4fa; engine test 332/332. Prior binary banked at tools/gcc-2.7.2/build/cc1.PRE-CRASHFIX-045c9543.",
    "maspsx_fingerprint": "2026-09-25 maspsx fingerprint fix (engine bug fix, no toolchain change): toolchain.maspsx_rev was `git -C tools/maspsx rev-parse HEAD`, but tools/maspsx is vendored with no .git, so it recorded the PARENT repo's HEAD (8454a511fa3032e66907e32196eebad60cfcc473, == the locked git_commit) and every later commit read as maspsx drift. Replaced by toolchain.maspsx_sources_sha1 = engine.oracle.maspsx_sources_sha1() (SHA1 over path+content of tools/maspsx/maspsx.py and tools/maspsx/maspsx/**/*.py, the code the build executes) = c1bb9a7d83e7fbd7090b546078afd9276aad2067. maspsx sources are unchanged: `git log` shows no tools/maspsx change after the previous lock. The re-lock also re-records the corpus hashes of src/ings.c and src/text1b.c, changed since the previous lock by the reviewed commits 89a3bc8aa (main) and bcbd223ba (func_80073C78).",
    "cc1_build_2026_09_25": "2026-09-25 narrow PLUS->IOR adoption (owner ruling bcdc1648e; docs/ORACLE-COMPILER.md 'Owner ruling 2026-09-25 (second batch)'): build/cc1 = `bash tools/build_oracle_cc1.sh --install` = pinned upstream decompals/mips-gcc-2.7.2@43d1cdb67ed135879869b5266f01efaaada5e35a + tools/cc1-reorg-negate-rtx-decl.patch (the 2026-08-24 crash fix, now a tracked recipe input) + tools/cc1-plus-to-ior-narrow.patch (replaces tools/cc1-no-plus-to-ior.patch); recipe all -O0 -g, combine.o -O, -fgnu89-inline (host gcc 13, x86_64). sha1 aa04d7619cd79215788d18d6870ebc6c8d1d822d, simplify_rtx 0x3a6a. Self-check: identical asm on all 34 TUs vs the retired no-rewrite compiler 0f438e42 (kept as build/cc1.PRE-RECIPE-0f438e42). Diagnostic tools/gcc-2.7.2/cc1 rebuilt with the same patch: 888dda6755596e3ac826c38c36be3103297cbac8, agrees on all 34 TUs. Verified: FULL BUILD SHA1 == 62efab4f73f992798c43e8c730aa43baa10bb4fa (verify-oracle --rebuild); engine test 720/720; fixtures 5/5; check_completion_integrity OK.",
    "maspsx_2026_09_26": "Q17 re-lock also records toolchain.maspsx_sources_sha1 c1bb9a7d -> 2063dcae: the committed maspsx change 56d7fba01 (accept an empty load/store offset `($REG)` as ASPSX 2.34 does; owner Q11, ae96881fc), the only tools/maspsx commit since the previous lock b65c5dba. No maspsx change in this commit. The same re-lock refreshes every corpus/config hash to the content staged in the Q17 commit: that churn is the commits landed since the previous lock b65c5dba (not only the maspsx change) plus this commit's src/ings.c revert."
